WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00.200 --> 00:05.220
Later this week, Aaliyah is planning to lead a kick-off meeting with the transformation team.

2
00:05.930 --> 00:11.360
She wants to make sure that she’s clear about her priorities, and that she uses the time efficiently.

3
00:11.910 --> 00:14.980
She’s thinking through the agenda and is feeling stuck.

4
00:15.620 --> 00:21.090
She calls David Fu, who is a MODA board member and an advisor to the transformation team.

5
00:21.960 --> 00:23.870
“David, hi — do you have a minute to chat?”

6
00:24.290 --> 00:26.166
“Hey, Aaliyah. Sure. How can I help?”

7
00:26.166 --> 00:32.756
“I’m trying to wrap my head around this team kick-off. There’s so much ground I want to cover, and I know I only have 30 minutes.”

8
00:32.756 --> 00:35.848
“Yeah, we’ve all been there before. What do you have so far?”

9
00:35.848 --> 00:37.470
“I’d like to get to five things:

10
00:37.800 --> 00:42.460
align on the scope of the transformation, identify the key deliverables, set deadlines,

11
00:42.460 --> 00:46.370
align on how we’ll work together — and, of course, get to know everyone.”

12
00:46.890 --> 00:48.990
“Oof, I really don’t want to rush this.”

13
00:50.050 --> 00:51.010
“David, what do I do?”

14
00:51.460 --> 00:54.660
“That sounds like a lot, Aaliyah. What are your top priorities?”

15
00:55.530 --> 01:01.410
“Hmm — my top priorities are making sure we start off on the right foot and get to know each other better.

16
01:01.830 --> 01:05.700
I also think the team is eager to hear how we’ll be working together over the next few months.

17
01:06.020 --> 01:09.950
And if we have time, I want to touch on the priority deliverables we have coming up soon.”

18
01:10.600 --> 01:11.650
“That sounds reasonable.

19
01:12.130 --> 01:18.400
It would be really helpful to think about what you want to get out of this meeting — and also what your team might need.”

20
01:18.980 --> 01:22.950
“Maybe try to gauge their needs, huh? Good point.

21
01:23.530 --> 01:26.790
Let me see if I can go catch someone from the team now and see what’s on their mind.”

22
01:27.750 --> 01:29.700
“Hey Noah, working late?”

23
01:30.210 --> 01:33.410
“Story of my life. I’m just quickly finishing up.

24
01:33.990 --> 01:36.350
My partner’s mum is visiting tonight for dinner.”

25
01:37.160 --> 01:39.590
“In that case, could I borrow five minutes of your time?”

26
01:40.100 --> 01:41.220
“Sure, what’s up?”

27
01:41.930 --> 01:47.170
“I’m a bit stuck. I’m thinking about tomorrow and trying to define the purpose of our transformation team kick-off.

28
01:47.720 --> 01:51.520
Can I walk you through the agenda and see if there’s anything else you or the team would like to add?”

